<%# Cookie Policy — lists only what BonID actually stores. Keep in sync with:
    session store (_bonid_session), Citizens::DeviceRecognition (bonid_device),
    pending_consent (sessions/registrations/oauth controllers), Devise
    rememberable (staff), the two dismissible banners, and the
    cookie_consent_controller (localStorage + optional analytics). %>
<% analytics = ENV["GA_MEASUREMENT_ID"].present? %>
<div class="terms-page container py-5">
  <div class="mx-auto" style="max-width: 800px;">

    <header class="mb-5 text-center">
      <h1 class="terms-title font-orbitron text-haitian-blue mb-3">Cookie Policy</h1>
      <p class="text-muted lead mx-auto" style="max-width: 640px;">
        What BonID stores in your browser, why, and how long it stays.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="terms-content">

      <section class="mb-5">
        <h3 class="terms-heading">1. What cookies are</h3>
        <p>
          Cookies are small files a website saves in your browser. BonID uses them mainly to keep
          you signed in and to protect your account. We do not use advertising cookies, and we
          never sell what they contain.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-5">
        <h3 class="terms-heading">2. Essential cookies</h3>
        <p>BonID cannot work without these, so they do not need your consent.</p>
        <div class="table-responsive">
          <table class="table table-sm align-top small">
            <thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Duration</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <td><code>_bonid_session</code></td>
                <td>Keeps you signed in, remembers your language and protects forms against forgery.</td>
                <td>Until you close the browser</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><code>bonid_device</code></td>
                <td>Recognizes devices you have signed in from, so we can alert you when a new device signs in to your account. Encrypted.</td>
                <td>Until you sign out of that device in Settings or clear your cookies</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><code>pending_consent</code></td>
                <td>Holds a partner's access request while you sign in, so you can approve or refuse it afterward. Encrypted.</td>
                <td>30 minutes, deleted once you answer</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><code>remember_*_token</code></td>
                <td>Staff portals only: keeps you signed in when you tick "Remember me".</td>
                <td>2 weeks</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-5">
        <h3 class="terms-heading">3. Preference cookies</h3>
        <p>These remember small choices so we don't ask again.</p>
        <div class="table-responsive">
          <table class="table table-sm align-top small">
            <thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Duration</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <td><code>legacy_cin_alert_dismissed</code></td>
                <td>Hides the old-CIN notice on your dashboard after you close it.</td>
                <td>7 days</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><code>cep_postponement_banner_dismissed</code></td>
                <td>Hides the election postponement notice after you close it.</td>
                <td>30 days</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><code>cookieConsent</code> (browser storage)</td>
                <td>Remembers your choice in the cookie banner.</td>
                <td>Until you change it or clear your browser data</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-5">
        <h3 class="terms-heading">4. Analytics cookies</h3>
        <% if analytics %>
          <p>
            Only if you allow them in the cookie banner, Google Analytics sets the cookies below to
            measure how BonID is used. If you don't allow them, nothing is loaded.
          </p>
          <div class="table-responsive">
            <table class="table table-sm align-top small">
              <thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Duration</th></tr></thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr><td><code>_ga</code>, <code>_ga_*</code></td><td>Counts visits and pages viewed (Google Analytics).</td><td>Up to 2 years</td></tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
        <% else %>
          <p>
            BonID does not currently use analytics cookies. If we add them, they will only run after
            you agree in the cookie banner, and we will list them here first.
          </p>
        <% end %>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-5">
        <h3 class="terms-heading">5. Managing your choices</h3>
        <p>
          You can change your cookie choices at any time:
          <a href="#" data-cookie-settings class="text-primary fw-semibold">open cookie settings</a>.
          You can also delete cookies from your browser settings; if you delete essential ones,
          you will be signed out and your devices will be treated as new.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-4">
        <h3 class="terms-heading">6. Contact us</h3>
        <p>
          Questions about cookies or your data:
          <a href="mailto:support@verifyem.ht" class="text-primary fw-semibold">support@verifyem.ht</a>.
          See also our <%= link_to "Privacy Policy", privacy_path, class: "text-primary fw-semibold" %>.
        </p>
      </section>

    </div>

    <p class="text-muted small text-center mt-5">
      Last updated: November 25, 2026
    </p>
  </div>
</div>
